From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:03:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: stub for functions the translator cannot lift, run
 through the JIT (blocker 1)

Aot(stub_unliftable=True) turns a function Remill cannot lift, or whose IR needs a runtime symbol that is
not defined, into a stub sub_<address>. A direct bl to it still links; the stub runs the function in the
JIT, or stops naming the address and the reason when there is no JIT. Default behaviour is unchanged
(LiftError / LinkError). A callee nobody supplied stays a LinkError. New counter unlifted_calls.
Found on the way: fadd/fmul/fdiv lift but need __remill_fpu_exception_clear/test, now stubbed too.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: a function Remill cannot lift blocked the build of all its direct callers; NX2Linux recompilation only
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch feat/teo-t4-jit-secours)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
